                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very average game. Yet it's a Lemmings-like game and the graphics are cute...\nThe gameplay seems simple on the surface: get spirits to the swirl. They move forward automatically, and you only have four possible transformations: dig, grow a branch, blow wind, or turn into a ball that blocks the wind.\nAdd to this a secondary objective: lighting up plants, by walking near them or dropping a light projectile from above.\n\nSimple? No, behind all this lies a deeply sadistic game:\nThe wind physics are often unpredictable, especially since multiple air currents frequently mix together. And spirits following one another might react differently within the same currents.  Add to that the transformations into balls that get stuck or bounce in equally unpredictable ways.\nThe game sometimes requires some thought, but even when the solution was obvious, I often found myself retrying the same sections over and over again.\nA rewind button might have slightly improved the gameplay experience.\n\nI can barely recommend it, Spirits is aimed primarily at masochists who enjoy a difficulty that shows no respect for the player.",
